			<item>
				<title>Essentia Spot</title>
				<link>https://bluevisual.tv/work/essentia-spot/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 14 Mar 2023 10:46:10 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://bluevisual.tv/work/essentia-spot/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;FLIP simulations for a short Essentia spot we were tasked with at Buck.&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-image&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;video width=&#34;960&#34; height=&#34;540&#34; autoplay loop muted controls&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;source src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/essentia-spot/essentia-spot-video-01.mp4&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/video&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;splash&#34;&gt;Splash&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-image&#34; oncontextmenu=&#34;return false;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;lightbox-toggle01&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/essentia-spot/essentia-spot-01.jpg&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; name=&#34;lightbox-toggle1&#34; id=&#34;lightbox-toggle01&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;lightbox&#34; oncontextmenu=&#34;return false;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;lightbox-toggle01&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/essentia-spot/essentia-spot-01.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I used a custom SOP microsolver to improve and give more elegant surface-tension dynamics.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-image&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;video width=&#34;960&#34; height=&#34;540&#34; autoplay loop muted controls&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;source src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/essentia-spot/essentia-spot-video-02.mp4&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/video&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;caption&#34;&gt;A visualization for an alternate splash. The colors represent particle travel distance.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;air-bubble&#34;&gt;Air Bubble&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I also did procedural dynamics for the air bubble inside the bottle which turned into a trickier process than I originally anticipated.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Aircover Spot</title>
				<link>https://bluevisual.tv/work/aircover-spot/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 14 Nov 2022 10:43:06 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://bluevisual.tv/work/aircover-spot/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Buck was tasked with creating spots for AirBnB&amp;rsquo;s Aircover, an insurance program for their hosts.&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;vimeo-container project-image&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;iframe width=&#34;960&#34; height=&#34;540&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/embed/HU-wFN42sMs&#34; title=&#34;YouTube video player&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share&#34; allowfullscreen&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;rain-system&#34;&gt;Rain System&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Similar to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/work/amazon-halo&#34;&gt;Amazon Halo Spot&lt;/a&gt;, we needed rain for this moody animation. In fact, I brought over the same system and tweaked it for our needs and added some additional controls.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There were many iterations on the look and feel of the rain drops, their splashes, and their puddles. Knowing this is always the case, the tool was designed for ultimate flexibility in mind, so it was easy to adjust. This is one of the many reasons I enjoy building and working with procedural systems instead of waiting and twiddling my thumbs for simulations to finish.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Amazon Halo</title>
				<link>https://bluevisual.tv/work/amazon-halo/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 26 Feb 2021 00:25:03 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://bluevisual.tv/work/amazon-halo/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;In this project, I was tasked with doing some rain effects for the Amazon Halo commercial.&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-image&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;video width=&#34;960&#34; height=&#34;540&#34; autoplay loop muted controls&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;source src=&#34;https://bluevisual.tv/project-media/amazon-halo/amazon-halo-spot.mp4&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/video&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;rain&#34;&gt;Rain&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;One of the asks was for a particular droplet splash that hits the product. It needed to be able to be timed precisely and generate physically accurate secondary droplets. Because I hate simulating things, I decided I would design a procedural system for this that was seamless with the background rain.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
